 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gain against current and temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At VCE = -5 V the typical gain is nearly flat from -1 mA to about -100 mA, around 250 at 25 °C and 340 at 100 °C, then falls off above about -300 mA; both curves come down to about 95 at -4 A (Fig.2)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Saturation",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "With the base driven at one tenth of the collector current, VCE(sat) is typically about -13 mV around -5 to -10 mA, about -60 mV at -500 mA and about -210 to -230 mV at -3 A, higher at 100 °C than at -25 °C above a few milliamps (Fig.3). VBE(sat) under the same drive runs from about -0.35 V (100 °C) and -0.47 V (-25 °C) at -0.1 mA to about -0.93 V and -0.98 V at -3 A (Fig.4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Base-emitter on voltage",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At VCE = -5 V, a collector current of -1 A takes a VBE of about -0.67 V at 100 °C and about -0.75 V at -25 °C (Fig.5)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Measured at 1 MHz, input capacitance Cib falls from about 710 pF at -0.1 V reverse bias to about 270 pF at -10 V, and output capacitance Cob from about 230 pF at -0.1 V to about 54 pF at -20 V (Fig.6)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Dissipation",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The typical junction-to-ambient thermal resistance of 42 °C/W is for the device with its collector lead on 52 mm × 52 mm of 2 oz copper on a single-sided 1.6 mm FR4 board, in still air at steady state."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and assembly",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The SOT-223 body uses a molding compound rated UL 94V-0 and is RoHS compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026. Moisture sensitivity is MSL 1 to J-STD-020, with lead-free reflow peaking at 260 °C. The top of the body is marked ZT955."
  }
 ],
